{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"agent_message","text":"1. Additional refactoring strategy used  \nExtracted one cohesive responsibility from `Element`: **selector/query + DOM finder operations** (`select*`, `selectNodes*`, `is`, `closest`, `selectXpath*`, and `getElementsBy*` family) into a new superclass so `Element` delegates through inheritance instead of directly implementing those methods.\n\n2. Files changed  \n- Added [ElementQueryOps.java](/data/henrique/langchain_prototype/codex/data/repositories/jsoup/src/main/java/org/jsoup/nodes/ElementQueryOps.java)  \n- Updated [Element.java](/data/henrique/langchain_prototype/codex/data/repositories/jsoup/src/main/java/org/jsoup/nodes/Element.java)\n\n3. Expected impact on the smell  \n- `Element` is simplified by removing a large query/finder method cluster from direct implementation.  \n- Public API behavior is preserved via inheritance.  \n- However, `Element` still likely remains above the stated thresholds (`public < 20`, `total < 30`): current rough declaration count is still much higher, so this extraction alone is unlikely to fully clear IM.\n\n4. Validation command executed  \nRan:  \n`mvn -q -Djapicmp.skip=true -Drat.skip=true -Dcheckstyle.skip=true -Dspotbugs.skip=true -Dpmd.skip=true -DskipITs clean verify`  \nResult: Java compilation passed after refactor; test phase failed due sandbox/network restrictions (`SocketException: Operation not permitted` when Netty tests attempt to bind sockets), not due compile errors from this refactor.\n\n5. Remaining risks  \n- Main risk: smell threshold still likely not met for `Element`; further decomposition is required.  \n- Runtime behavior risk is low for moved methods (logic was moved verbatim), but full test confirmation is blocked in this environment by socket restrictions."}}
